course: dictionary
lesson: 2795
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Display» is one of them. It can be a thing you look at (a noun) or an action of showing something (a verb). The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «At a firework display, stand behind the barrier, because fireworks can burn and injure people who are too close.» Here a display is a show. The clues are firework and stand behind the barrier: people watch from a safe place.
explain: «The Romans wrote their laws on twelve tablets displayed in the forum.» Displayed means shown so people could see them. Try your meaning in the sentence: «wrote their laws on twelve tablets shown in the forum» still makes sense, so you have found it.
fact: A display can be a noun (a display, displays) or a verb (to display, displayed, displaying).
fact: A display is a collection of things arranged for people to look at, such as a wall display of pupils' work.
fact: To display something is to show it so people can see it, such as displaying results in a table or on a graph.
fact: The display on a phone, computer or calculator is its screen.
fact: Animals can display too: a peacock spreads its tail to attract a mate.
exercise: «Our class work is on the wall display in the hall.» What is a wall display? | A box for storing paper | A painted fence | A loud noise made by the wall | *Work pinned up so people can look at it
exercise: «The science results were displayed in a table.» What does displayed mean? | Thrown away | Hidden under a book | Counted twice | *Shown clearly so people can read them
exercise: «The phone's display was cracked.» What is the display? | *The screen | A phone case | The battery | A game played on the phone
test: «The peacock opened its tail to display to the females.» What does display mean here? | Hide | Shake | *Show off to attract a mate | Sleep
test: What does the phrase «on display» mean? | Lost or hidden | Broken and thrown away | *Shown for people to look at | Sold quickly to the highest bidder
exam: «The calculator display showed 42.» What is a calculator display? | *The screen that shows the numbers | A carrying case | A set of buttons | A small battery
